      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I do commissions for commissioners who don't know how to or don't want to upload the world themselves. And I wouldn't be able to upload to their account without them giving me their account credentials, which is insecure. I know avatar creators face the same issue making avatars for others.\n\nA co-creator system would be a solution. They could add me as co-creator and then I could do the upload.\n\nThis idea implies similar features to groups. Like you'd need a \"primary creator\" like a group owner. They'd want to be able to remove co-creators. Ideally also you'd be able to transfer who's the primary creator, for example if they wanted to pass off maintaining a world to someone else.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
